  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF TIGERS THROUGH LAW ENFORCEMENT AND PREY POPULATION RECOVERY IN DONG PHAYAYEN KHAO YAI FOREST COMPLEX, THAILAND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to solidify the recovery of tigers in Thailand&apos;s Dong Phayayen-Khao Yai (DPKY) Forest Complex and secure the dispersal to connected environs including Bantaey Chhmar Protected Landscape (BCPL) in Cambodia. Project objectives are as follows: (1) Improve strategic enforcement in DPKY and BCPL; (2) Expand monitoring to increase understanding of tiger population dynamics and dispersal to connected habitat; and (3) Expand wider support for the conservation of tigers, prey and biodiversity in DPKY, BCPL and the Dangrak ecological corridor.</narrative>
  </description>
